      "part_type": "Hadith",
      "path": "/books/al-kafi:5:3:95:4",
      "text": [
        " سُئِلَ أَبُو عَبْدِ اللَّهِ ( عليه السلام ) عَنِ الْمُتْعَةِ أَ هِيَ مِنَ الْأَرْبَعِ فَقَالَ لَا وَ لَا مِنَ السَّبْعِينَ ."
      ],
      "translations": {
        "en.hubeali": [
          "Al Husayn Bin Muhammad, from Moalla Bin Muhammad, from Al Hassan Bin Ali, from Hammad Bin Usman, from Abu Baseer who said, ",
          "‘Abu Abdullah<sup>asws</sup> was asked about the <span class=\"iTxt\">Mut’a</span>, is she from the four (allowable wives)?’ So he<sup>asws</sup> said: ‘No, nor from the seventy (i.e. as many as you so desire to)’."
        ],
        "en.sarwar": [
          "4. Al-Husayn from Muhammad has narrated from Mu’alla’ ibn Muhammad from al-Hassan ibn Ali from Hammad ibn ‘Uthaman from abu Basir who has said the following: “This is concerning my question before abu ‘Abd Allah, ‘Alayhi al-Salam, if al-Mut‘ah (advantageous marriage) is of four. He (the Imam) said, ‘No, even seventy is not unlawful.’” "
        ]
      }
    },
